{"seed_id": "BigCodeBench/232", "verdict": "update", "note": "test case inconsistency", "author": "author_2", "prompt": "You are given transaction records describing customer purchases. Each record has a customer name, a purchase category, and a sales amount. Read all input from standard input and write the required summary to standard output.\n\nInput format:\n- The first line contains a single token that should be a non-negative integer N, the number of transaction records that follow.\n- If this first token cannot be parsed as a non-negative integer, the input is considered invalid; in that case print exactly the line `Invalid input` and stop (do not print anything else).\n- Otherwise, each of the next N lines contains a record in the form `Customer,Category,Sales`, where `Customer` and `Category` are strings (containing no commas) and `Sales` is an integer.\n\nProcessing rules:\n- If the same customer name appears more than once, keep only the first occurrence of that customer (in the order the records appear) and discard the later ones.\n- Compute the total sales as the sum of the `Sales` values from the retained (deduplicated) records.\n- Determine the most popular category as the category that occurs most often among the retained records. If two or more categories are tied for the highest frequency, choose the one that comes first alphabetically.\n- If N is 0 (no records), the total sales is 0 and there is no popular category; in that case print `Total Sales: 0` and `Most Popular Category: None`.\n\nOutput format:\nPrint exactly two lines:\n```\nTotal Sales: <total>\nMost Popular Category: <category>\n```\nwhere `<total>` is the computed integer total sales and `<category>` is the determined most popular category (or `None` as described above).\n\nExample:\nInput:\n```\n4\nJohn,Electronics,500\nMary,Home,300\nPeter,Beauty,400\nNick,Sports,600\n```\nOutput:\n```\nTotal Sales: 1800\nMost Popular Category: Beauty\n```"}
